Mechanism: If there were earlier timeouts, they are not reproducible now; the forwarding path and routing adjacencies are up and passing traffic normally.

Localization: End-to-end Office (192.168.3.0/24) to Internet Lab (128.168.0.0/16) across router1–router2—no faulty interface or daemon found.

Root cause: No network-side fault present at the time of investigation; earlier issues were transient or outside the routed path.

Corrective fix: No changes required. Please re-test from affected Office PCs. If symptoms recur, note exact time, source/destination IPs, and whether hostname vs. IP was used so we can check for transient endpoint/DNS issues while they occur. We will continue to monitor. 
